========================================================================================
ARCHITECTURE OVERVIEW
========================================================================================
This blueprint implements a Zero-Leak, Protected Admin Debug Tab via PySide6 & FastAPI.
It covers the full stack across 5 phases, starting with JWT authentication and credential
hardening, building through backend admin endpoints, client login dialog, and concluding
with a conditionally-injected admin diagnostics panel that is NEVER compiled at app boot.

Tech Stack:
  - Backend:  FastAPI (Python 3.9 strict)
  - Client:   PySide6 (Qt for Python)
  - Security: passlib[bcrypt] + python-jose (JWT)
  - Database: SQLite / PostgreSQL (existing repository pattern)
  - Queue:    Celery + Redis (existing, for diagnostics endpoint)
  - Auth:     OPERION_ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH (bcrypt) + JWT Bearer tokens

========================================================================================
PHASE 0: CREDENTIAL HARDENING + JWT AUTHENTICATION FOUNDATION
========================================================================================
OBJECTIVE: Replace plaintext admin password with bcrypt hash, implement JWT + RBAC.
DEPENDENCIES: None. This is the foundation.
LINT/TYPECHECK: ruff check, mypy (if configured)

========================================================================================
TASK 0.1 — One-Time Hash Script (Created → Run → Deleted)
========================================================================================
FILE: scripts/hash_admin_password.py (EPHEMERAL — deleted after one use)

  LIFECYCLE:
    1. Developer creates scripts/hash_admin_password.py
    2. Developer runs it once: python scripts/hash_admin_password.py
    3. Terminal prints the bcrypt hash (e.g. $2b$12$...)
    4. Developer copies the hash into admin.env as OPERION_ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH=<hash>
    5. Developer deletes scripts/hash_admin_password.py from the repo

  CONTENTS (approx 15 lines, no imports from codebase):
    from passlib.context import CryptContext
    ctx = CryptContext(schemes=["bcrypt"])
    TARGET_PASSWORD = "THE ACTUAL ADMIN PASSWORD HERE"
    print(ctx.hash(TARGET_PASSWORD))

  GUARANTEE: The plaintext password exists only in (a) developer memory, (b) the deleted
  script file. It NEVER reaches admin.env, source code, logs, or API responses.

