========================================================================================
TASK 0.3 — Create backend/security.py
========================================================================================
FILE: backend/security.py (NEW)

  Two subsystems, Python 3.9 strict type hints (typing.Dict, typing.Optional, etc.):

  A. passlib CryptContext (bcrypt):
     verify_password(plain_password: str, hashed_password: str) -> bool
     hash_password(password: str) -> str  # used only by the one-time script

  B. python-jose JWT:
     create_access_token(data: typing.Dict, expires_delta: typing.Optional[timedelta]=None) -> str
     decode_access_token(token: str) -> typing.Dict[str, typing.Any]  # raises JWTError on failure

  JWT payload: {"sub": email, "role": role, "exp": expiry_epoch}

========================================================================================
TASK 0.4 — Create backend/api/v1/auth.py
========================================================================================
FILE: backend/api/v1/auth.py (NEW)

  Route: POST /api/v1/auth/token
  Dependency: OAuth2PasswordRequestForm

  AUTH FLOW (refactored per credential hardening):
    1. Extract email + plaintext password from form body
    2. Compare incoming email against OPERION_ADMIN_EMAIL
    3. IF match → call verify_password(plain_pw, OPERION_ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH):
         - True:  issue JWT with {"sub": admin_email, "role": "admin"}
                  ⚠ ZERO DATABASE ACCESS for admin login
         - False: raise HTTP 401 Unauthorized
    4. IF no match → fall through to parameterized DB users table lookup:
         - Query users table by email
         - Verify bcrypt hash
         - Issue JWT with {"sub": user_email, "role": user_role}
         - Or HTTP 401

  ⚠ bcrypt verify_password is CPU-bound. Wrap in:
     await loop.run_in_executor(None, verify_password, plain_pw, stored_hash)

  Return: {"access_token": "<token>", "token_type": "bearer"}

========================================================================================
TASK 0.4a — Ensure users table exists (optional future-proofing)
========================================================================================
FILE: database/schema.py (MODIFIED, optional)

  Add table: users(id, email UNIQUE, password_hash, role DEFAULT 'dispatcher',
                   is_active DEFAULT 1, created_at)
  NOTE: Not required for admin panel. Admin auth bypasses DB entirely.

========================================================================================
TASK 0.5 — Create backend/dependencies/security.py
========================================================================================
FILE: backend/dependencies/security.py (NEW)
FILE: backend/dependencies/__init__.py (NEW)

  Three FastAPI dependency factories using OAuth2PasswordBearer(tokenUrl="/api/v1/auth/token"):

  get_current_user():
    - Extract Bearer token from Authorization header
    - Decode JWT via decode_access_token()
    - If sub == OPERION_ADMIN_EMAIL → return in-memory dict:
        {"id": 0, "email": admin_email, "role": "admin", "is_admin": True}
      ⚠ ZERO DATABASE ACCESS for admin identity
    - Else query users table, return user dict
    - HTTP 401 on invalid/expired token

  require_admin():
    - Calls get_current_user()
    - Asserts "role" == "admin"
    - HTTP 403 Forbidden if not admin

  require_dispatcher():
    - Calls get_current_user()
    - Asserts "role" in ("admin", "dispatcher")
    - HTTP 403 Forbidden otherwise

